What this check does NOT catch:
  - A family that generates SOME reactions but the wrong products for a given entry.
    That needs the declared products compared against what the recipe makes, which is
    probe_producibility.py; this check is the cheap always-on version.
  - Families with no training set at all. They are skipped, not passed.
  - Products beyond the FIRST generation. A product of a product is not driven back in.
  - Anything beyond the first 25 entries of a family.

